<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yoshino, Nara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yoshino is a mountain town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a> Prefecture, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, famous for the cherry trees of Mount Yoshino and for its shrines and temples on the pilgrimage routes of the Kii Mountains. In 1336 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-daigo">Emperor Go-Daigo</a> fled there with the imperial regalia and set up the Southern Court, which rivalled the Northern Court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> until 1392.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yoshino-nara.jpg" alt="Yoshino, Nara" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 水だらけのプール · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yoshino_Montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
